# GitHub reads this file and shows a "Cite this repository" button.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use sway-eval, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "sway-eval: Auditing Order Sensitivity in AI Decision Models"
abstract: >-
  sway-eval measures, on a deployer's own records and without labels, how often
  the order in which a record presents its sections decides a decision model's
  verdict, prices that sensitivity as a Brier cost, compares defenses
  (canonical layouts, balanced Williams sets, an adaptive screen) by calls and
  agreement, and checks hosted models for run-to-run noise and serving changes.
authors:
  - given-names: Ramin
    family-names: Zandvakili
    affiliation: Independent Researcher
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-4638-0012"
  - given-names: Nasim
    family-names: Eshgarf
    affiliation: University of Minnesota
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-13"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/raminzandvakili/sway-eval"
keywords:
  - decision models
  - System One models
  - LLM evaluation
  - calibration
  - order sensitivity
  - fairness
  - robustness
